    "sourceWikitext": "{{recipesummary\n| category = Vegetarian recipes\n| servings = 3–4\n| time = 15 minutes\n| difficulty = 1\n}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian cuisine]]\n\n'''Cauliflower with breadcrumbs''' is a popular dish and side-dish in Poland and many parts of Central Europe. It's really simple to make.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 head of [[Cookbook:Cauliflower|cauliflower]]\n* 50 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]]\n* 2–3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Bread Crumb|breadcrumbs]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] fresh [[Cookbook:Dill|dill]] (optional)\n \n==Procedure==\n#[[Cookbook:Boiling|Boil]] the cauliflower for about 10 minutes.\n#Melt some butter in the [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] or a [[Cookbook:Microwave|microwave]].\n#Mix the butter with the breadcrumbs, and add dill if using.\n#Drain the cauliflower and add the mixture on top.  \n#Eat!\n\n\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Side dish recipes]]\n[[Category:Boiled recipes]]\n[[Category:Polish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cauliflower]]\n[[Category:Recipes using bread crumb]]\n[[Category:Recipes using dill]]",
